5,1,1,talk,Shizue,,"Good morning, everyone. I’m glad we’re all here. Let’s begin by sharing our initial thoughts on the proposals.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,I prefer we verify operational capacity before judging scientific merit. Who is actually available to run these projects?,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Victoria,,I agree with Ryuji. We must assess if shared infrastructure can absorb this workload without failing.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I’d like to understand the financial baseline first. Which costs does the agency still cover centrally, versus what the awardee must absorb?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Midori,,"I’m a bit shy, but I worry about non-scientific interruptions. Can we check where work actually gets delayed?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Shizue,,"Thank you, Midori. Your concern is very valid. Let’s see if we can find where those delays truly originate.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Midori, delays often mask staffing gaps. I need to know if the technical posts are actually filled or just listed on paper.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"I suspect the bottleneck isn't just people, but the physical systems they rely on. We need to verify if the shared facilities are actually accredited and booked correctly.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Victoria, that’s a fair point. But if the agency’s central absorption of costs is shrinking, your infrastructure might be underfunded regardless of accreditation.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Midori,,I appreciate your insights. I’ll look into incident logs and closeout files to see where non-scientific delays actually occur.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Shizue,,"I’m thinking about the closeout files too. It’s important to see what finished awards actually delivered, not just what was promised.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Shizue, closeouts show past performance, not current availability. I need to verify if the technical staff listed are actually present and working now.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"Ryuji, presence is vital, but without accredited facilities, those staff have nowhere to work. I’ll check the accreditation and bookings.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,I’ll examine the national computing agreement and the portfolio review of schedule overruns to map where costs are shifting.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Midori,,I’ll check the national repository deposit turnaround and incident logs. I want to see if administrative bottlenecks are slowing down the actual science.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Shizue,,I’ll look into the closeout files and the portfolio review of schedule overruns. I want to see what actually happened before.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will examine the staffing rolls for technical posts and the minutes on secondments. I need to confirm who is genuinely present and working now.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Victoria,,"I will examine the accreditation and bookings at shared facilities, and the incident logs on shared instrumentation.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I’ll review the travel and bench-fee ledgers, plus the national computing agreement. I need to see exactly where the agency’s central cost absorption is eroding.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Midori,,I’ll review the incident logs on shared instrumentation and the national repository deposit turnaround. I want to pinpoint exactly where administrative friction disrupts the science.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
