35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I found that catalogue-style awards still draw users a decade later, while mechanism-focused ones often stall. We should value sustained utility over quick answers.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The phenotyping technicians are gone, but the glasshouse crew remains. I need to know if the seconded analysts return before the grant starts.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The spectroscopy suite sat idle for eleven weeks. That’s a critical failure point. We cannot fund projects relying on that equipment without a guaranteed service contract.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The computing agreement covers simulations free, but animal-unit rates spiked. I need to know if the agency still absorbs those central costs or if they’re now on the awardee.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The repository turnaround improved to weeks, which is great. But the spectroscopy suite’s eleven-week idle period worries me. How do we prevent that?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"Midori, that idle period is troubling. My closeout data shows mechanism-focused projects often stall. We must ensure the infrastructure supports sustained, practical utility.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Victoria, the glasshouse crew is intact, but the modelling analysts are gone until autumn. Can we rely on the remaining staff to bridge that gap?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"Ryuji, the glasshouse is booked solid, but the spectroscopy gap remains. We must prioritize candidates who don’t depend on that broken service chain.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Victoria, the free computing hours are a genuine central subsidy. But the animal-unit spike suggests the agency is offloading biological costs onto the awardee.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,I agree with Victoria. We should prioritize candidates who don’t depend on that broken service chain. It’s safer for the science.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"Benjamin, your point about cost-shifting is vital. My data shows biological projects overrun twice as often. We must weigh that financial risk carefully.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"Benjamin, cost-shifting is real, but my concern is personnel. If the analysts don’t return, the project stalls regardless of funding.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"Benjamin, the cost shift is real, but the idle spectroscopy suite is a hard stop. We cannot fund projects dependent on that broken chain.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Shizue, your data aligns with my ledger findings. The agency is clearly offloading biological costs. We must penalize proposals relying on those inflated, awardee-borne rates.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I worry about the personnel gap too. If analysts are missing, the science stalls. We need a plan to bridge that autumn gap.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I’m glad we’re converging. Let’s wait for the candidates to see which ones truly fit our shared concerns about stability and utility.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree. We must match the grant to the staff actually present now, not the ones promised for later.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I concur. We must select a candidate whose workflow bypasses the idle spectroscopy suite entirely. Stability is non-negotiable.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I agree. We must prioritize candidates whose workflows avoid the inflated, awardee-borne biological costs. Stability is key.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. We need a candidate whose work isn’t disrupted by these administrative or staffing gaps. Let’s see who fits that stability profile.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
